{"name":"Parrot Waxcap","hex":"#f8dc74","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parrot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of bird, many species of which are colorful and able to mimic human speech, of the order Psittaciformes or (narrowly) of the family Psittacidae.","A parroter; a person who repeats the words or ideas of others."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To repeat (exactly what has just been said) without necessarily showing understanding, in the manner of a parrot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parrot"},{"term":"waxcap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any agaric mushroom of the family Hygrophoraceae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waxcap"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gliophorus psittacinus","blocks":[{"text":"Gliophorus psittacinus, commonly known as the parrot toadstool or parrot waxcap, is a colourful mushroom that is a member of the genus Gliophorus. It was formerly known as Hygrocybe psittacina, but a molecular phylogenetics study found it to belong in the genus Gliophorus. It had already been placed in Gliophorus, but it had been considered a synonym of Hygrocybe. It has a cosmopolitan distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Hygrocybe_psittacina_54530.jpg/330px-Hygrocybe_psittacina_54530.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gliophorus_psittacinus","wikidata":"Q54366473"},{"title":"Parrot","blocks":[{"text":"Parrots, also known as psittacines from the name of the type genus Psittacus, are birds with a strong curved beak, upright stance, and clawed feet. They are classified in four families that contain roughly 410 species in 101 genera, found mostly in tropical and subtropical regions. The four families are the Psittaculidae, Psittacidae, Cacatuidae (cockatoos), and Strigopidae. One-third of all parrot species are threatened by extinction, with a higher aggregate extinction risk than any other comparable bird group. Parrots have a generally pantropical distribution with several species inhabiting temperate regions as well. The greatest diversity of parrots is in South America and Australasia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Rainbow_lorikeet_%28Trichoglossus_moluccanus_moluccanus%29_Sydney.jpg/330px-Rainbow_lorikeet_%28Trichoglossus_moluccanus_moluccanus%29_Sydney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parrot","wikidata":"Q31431"},{"title":"Hygrocybe","blocks":[{"text":"Hygrocybe is a genus of agarics in the family Hygrophoraceae. Called waxcaps in English, basidiocarps are often brightly coloured and have dry to waxy caps, white spores, and smooth, ringless stems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/2011-06-17_Hygrocybe_cantharellus_69428_cropped.jpg/330px-2011-06-17_Hygrocybe_cantharellus_69428_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hygrocybe","wikidata":"Q520530"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Faroe_stamp_306_hygrocybe_psittacina.jpg/500px-Faroe_stamp_306_hygrocybe_psittacina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Faroe_stamp_306_hygrocybe_psittacina.jpg/500px-Faroe_stamp_306_hygrocybe_psittacina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"On Faroe Islands stamp","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFaroe_stamp_306_hygrocybe_psittacina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parrot_range_2026.png/500px-Parrot_range_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parrot_range_2026.